  <text>
    <body>
      <p><hi rend="italic">The Leader</hi> of <ref target="http://nla.gov.au/nla.news-article198370105">8 November 1913</ref> recorded the death of John Henry Greenlees aged 59 at his residence 63 Madeline Street. John was the son of wine and spirit merchant Richard Greenlees of Wigan in Lancashire. He had been a resident of Carlton for 40 years. He was survived by his wife Amelia Frances (née Edwards, married 1873), and children Harry, Bert, Sarah, Fuchsia, Richard, Florrie (Florence, who had married Richard Reed in 1912), William and Arthur. Electoral rolls and directories from 1895 to 1925 show the occupation of members of the family.</p>
